#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""git-b3: Smuggle BLAKE3 Merkle integrity hashes into standard Git repositories.

Drop this executable onto your $PATH to use it as `git b3 <command>`:
  git b3 commit [-S] [-m <msg>] [-a] [--allow-empty] ...
  git b3 seal-head [--sign]
  git b3 tag [-a] [-s] <name> [target] [-m <msg>]
  git b3 verify [rev] [--expect <64-hex>] [--require-signature] [--allow-shallow]
  git b3 id [rev]
  git b3 log [-n <count>] [rev]
  git b3 install-hook [--force]

Zero external dependencies (uses native `blake3` package if installed, otherwise
falls back to the built-in C2SP-compliant pure-Python BLAKE3 implementation).
See SPEC.md for the normative specification.
"""

